# A lowercase declaration of another module written qualified (Semantics ch. 6: every
# declaration of a module is reachable by its qualified name; Jimmy's ruling QN: a
# qualified name needs no `use`). `Words.base` names the module's `let`, not a field of a
# value `Words`, since no value `Words` is in scope and a module is. Written by Claude on
# the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
mod Words
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Words.base} {Words.Twice Words.base} {Words.pair.left}")     # 0
